{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg5ywNn4rAbokQoEyYGsX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01F7zMSwWKyJL4jzM5ithwNJ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json,re\np='reference/coverage/metadata-forensics.md'; s=open(p).read()\ndef rep(old,new,cnt=1):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(old)==cnt, (old[:70], s.count(old)); s=s.replace(old,new)\nrep(\"(as of D15, 2026-10-15)\",\"(as of D16, 2026-10-16)\")\nrep(\"\"\"plus deeper fields of already-seen families (timed kits are cumulative, D15 added cross-file synthesis).\"\"\",\n\"\"\"plus deeper fields of already-seen families (timed kits are cumulative, D15 added cross-file synthesis).\n**D16 turned to e-mail** (`email.message_id` of one `.eml`; flavor \"replies, forwards, duplicates, reconstructed\nmessages ... stable message identities\"). PE stayed three days (D9-11) with a deeper field each day, so D17-D19 most\nplausibly ask deeper `email.*` fields (In-Reply-To / References / attachments / Received / auth) or a sibling mail\ncontainer (MBOX, Outlook MSG), then cross-message threading as a synthesis question. GM fmt word is `email`, not `eml`.\"\"\")\n# row 16 synthesis\ns=re.sub(r\"\\| 16 \\| Synthesis: `metadata-day-NN-synthesis-sha256-order` \\| seen D15 \\|\",\n \"| 16 | Synthesis: `metadata-day-NN-synthesis-sha256-order` | seen D15, D16 (`lib.meta.synthesis.digest_order`) |\", s)\n# row 74\nrep(\"| 74 | EML headers: Received chain (first hop/IP), Message-ID, Return-Path, X-Mailer, Date, Subject (RFC 2047), attachment names, DKIM `d=` | gap |\",\n    \"| 74 | EML headers: Received chain (first hop/IP), Message-ID, Return-Path, X-Mailer, Date, Subject (RFC 2047), attachment names, DKIM `d=` | seen D16 `email.message_id` (verbatim WITH `<>`); rest prebuilt eml -- registered as fmt `eml`, GM says `email` (gap email-fmt-alias) |\")\nrep(\"| high -- phishing staple |\",\"| high -- deeper `email.*` fields D17+ |\")\n# status refresh for rows built per .run/prebuild-state.json\nupd={26:\"prebuilt evtx\",29:\"prebuilt regf\",35:\"prebuilt prefetch\",36:\"prebuilt recycle\",37:\"prebuilt jumplist\",\n     39:\"prebuilt mft\",42:\"prebuilt task\",46:\"prebuilt pe\",47:\"prebuilt pe\",48:\"prebuilt pe\",49:\"prebuilt pe + x509\",\n     54:\"prebuilt vba\",57:\"prebuilt rtf\",58:\"prebuilt onenote\",61:\"prebuilt jpeg\",64:\"prebuilt gif/bmp/ico/wav\",\n     66:\"prebuilt mp3/wav (FLAC gap)\",67:\"prebuilt gzip\",76:\"prebuilt sqlite\",78:\"prebuilt pcap\",80:\"prebuilt x509\",\n     82:\"prebuilt elf\",83:\"prebuilt macho\"}\nlines=s.split('\\n')\nfor i,l in enumerate(lines):\n    m=re.match(r\"\\| (\\d+) \\|\",l)\n    if m and int(m.group(1)) in upd:\n        cells=l.split(' | ')\n        cells[2]=upd[int(m.group(1))]\n        lines[i]=' | '.join(cells)\ns='\\n'.join(lines)\nrows=\"\"\"| 86 | E-mail threading: In-Reply-To, References (list), thread root, Re:/Fwd: normalized subject, Thread-Index/Thread-Topic, Resent-Message-ID, duplicate Message-IDs | gap (email-threading) | flavor \"replies, forwards, duplicates\"; headers `In-Reply-To:`/`References:` | `msg['References'].split()` (stdlib `email`); root = first References id else In-Reply-To else own Message-ID | high -- D16 flavor promised it |\n| 87 | MIME structure: part count, Content-Type/boundary, transfer encodings, attachment names + decoded sizes/hashes, declared type vs magic | gap (email-mime-attachments) | `multipart/*`, `Content-Disposition: attachment`, base64 parts | `msg.walk()`, `part.get_payload(decode=True)`, `hashlib` | high |\n| 88 | E-mail auth: Authentication-Results spf/dkim/dmarc, ARC count, DKIM h=, Reply-To / Return-Path vs From domain mismatch | gap (email-auth-results) | `Authentication-Results:`, `ARC-Seal:`, `DKIM-Signature:` | regex over unfolded headers | med |\n| 89 | MBOX / mailbox export: message count, Message-IDs in order, duplicates, thread groups | gap (mbox-c